{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "synqlien-user-management-v1",
    "name": "LegalSynq SynqLien - User Management",
    "description": "Backend-only Postman workflow for Identity-owned SynqLien user management.\n\nImport `synqlien-user-management.postman_environment.json`, set `tenantCode`, `adminEmail`, `adminPassword`, and `targetPassword`, then run the collection in order. The login request captures `bearerToken`; invitation requests capture `userId`, `invitationId`, and the development-only `inviteToken`; user detail and mutation responses capture `accessVersion` for `If-Match`.\n\nGateway-visible base: `http://localhost:5010/identity`. To call Identity directly, change `identityBaseUrl` to `http://localhost:5001`.\n\nRequired caller: `TenantAdmin`, `PlatformAdmin`, or a user with `SYNQLIEN_USER_ADMIN`. The fixed product is `SYNQ_LIENS`; tenant and actor IDs come from the JWT and are never accepted from request bodies.\n\nThe main lifecycle uses a generated `@example.test` address when `targetEmail` is empty: invite, resend, accept, read, replace roles, revoke access, and grant access. The cancellation folder generates a separate user so it can exercise cancellation without conflicting with the accepted invitation.\n\nThe accept request is skipped when `inviteToken` or `targetPassword` is unavailable. Production responses intentionally suppress raw invitation tokens; copy the token from the delivered activation link into the environment if acceptance must be tested there. Mutation folders create or modify tenant users, so run them against production only with explicit authorization and intentional test data. Do not export or share the populated environment after it has captured credentials or tokens.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{bearerToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 - Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login as User Administrator",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Login succeeded', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.expect(json.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "pm.environment.set('bearerToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "if ((pm.environment.get('autoGenerateEmails') || 'true').toLowerCase() === 'true') {",
                  "  const stamp = Date.now();",
                  "  pm.environment.set('targetEmail', `postman.liens.${stamp}@example.test`);",
                  "  pm.environment.set('cancelTargetEmail', `postman.liens.cancel.${stamp}@example.test`);",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('userId');",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('invitationId');",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('inviteToken');",
                  "  pm.environment.unset('cancelInvitationId');",
                  "  pm.environment.set('accessVersion', '0');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\",\n  \"tenantCode\": \"{{tenantCode}}\",\n  \"resolveByEmail\": false,\n  \"portalProductCode\": \"SYNQ_LIENS\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticates the administrator and stores `accessToken` as `bearerToken`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 - Catalog and Directory",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List Assignable Roles",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Roles returned', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const codes = pm.response.json().items.map(role => role.code);",
                  "pm.expect(codes).to.include.members(['SYNQLIEN_SELLER', 'SYNQLIEN_BUYER', 'SYNQLIEN_HOLDER', 'SYNQLIEN_USER_ADMIN']);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/roles",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "roles"]
            },
            "description": "Permission: `SYNQ_LIENS.user_role:assign`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Users",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('User page returned', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.expect(json.items).to.be.an('array');",
                  "pm.expect(json.page).to.eql(Number(pm.environment.get('page')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/users?page={{page}}&pageSize={{pageSize}}",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "users"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "{{page}}" },
                { "key": "pageSize", "value": "{{pageSize}}" },
                { "key": "search", "value": "{{targetEmail}}", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "status", "value": "Granted", "disabled": true },
                { "key": "roleCode", "value": "{{inviteRoleCode}}", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Permission: `SYNQ_LIENS.user:read`. Optional filters are present but disabled."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 - Invitation Lifecycle",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Invite New User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('targetEmail')) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('targetEmail', `postman.liens.${Date.now()}@example.test`);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Invitation created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('userId', json.userId);",
                  "if (json.invitationId) pm.environment.set('invitationId', json.invitationId);",
                  "if (json.inviteToken) pm.environment.set('inviteToken', json.inviteToken);",
                  "pm.expect(json.email).to.eql(pm.environment.get('targetEmail'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{targetEmail}}\",\n  \"firstName\": \"{{targetFirstName}}\",\n  \"lastName\": \"{{targetLastName}}\",\n  \"phone\": \"{{targetPhone}}\",\n  \"roleCodes\": [\"{{inviteRoleCode}}\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/invitations",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "invitations"]
            },
            "description": "Permission: `SYNQ_LIENS.user:invite`. A new/inactive user receives a product-aware invitation; an existing active tenant user is granted access immediately."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Resend Invitation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Invitation resent', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('invitationId', json.invitationId);",
                  "if (json.inviteToken) pm.environment.set('inviteToken', json.inviteToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/invitations/{{invitationId}}/resend",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "invitations", "{{invitationId}}", "resend"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes the pending invitation, creates a replacement with the same role grants, and captures its new token in Development."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Accept Invitation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const inviteToken = pm.environment.get('inviteToken');",
                  "const targetPassword = pm.environment.get('targetPassword');",
                  "if (!inviteToken || !targetPassword) {",
                  "  console.warn('inviteToken or targetPassword is unavailable; skipping acceptance. Set both values before running this request.');",
                  "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Invitation accepted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"token\": \"{{inviteToken}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"{{targetPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/auth/accept-invite",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "accept-invite"]
            },
            "description": "Anonymous activation endpoint. Password activation, invitation acceptance, product access, roles, and access-version change commit atomically."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List Invitation History",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Invitation history returned', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.expect(pm.response.json().items).to.be.an('array');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/invitations?page={{page}}&pageSize={{pageSize}}",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "invitations"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "page", "value": "{{page}}" },
                { "key": "pageSize", "value": "{{pageSize}}" },
                { "key": "status", "value": "Accepted", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Permission: `SYNQ_LIENS.user:invite`. Status accepts Pending, Accepted, Expired, or Revoked."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 - Access and Roles",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get User Detail and ETag",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('User detail returned', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const etag = pm.response.headers.get('ETag');",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessVersion', etag ? etag.replace(/W\\//i, '').replace(/\"/g, '') : json.accessVersion);",
                  "pm.expect(json.id).to.eql(pm.environment.get('userId'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/users/{{userId}}",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "users", "{{userId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Permission: `SYNQ_LIENS.user:read`. Captures the ETag/access version required by mutations."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Replace Direct Roles",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Roles replaced', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const etag = pm.response.headers.get('ETag');",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessVersion', etag ? etag.replace(/W\\//i, '').replace(/\"/g, '') : json.accessVersion);",
                  "pm.expect(json.roles.map(role => role.code)).to.include(pm.environment.get('replacementRoleCode'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "If-Match", "value": "\"{{accessVersion}}\"" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"roleCodes\": [\"{{replacementRoleCode}}\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/users/{{userId}}/roles",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "users", "{{userId}}", "roles"]
            },
            "description": "Permission: `SYNQ_LIENS.user_role:assign`. Replaces direct roles only; inherited group roles are read-only."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Revoke Direct Product Access",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Direct access revoked', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const etag = pm.response.headers.get('ETag');",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessVersion', etag ? etag.replace(/W\\//i, '').replace(/\"/g, '') : json.accessVersion);",
                  "pm.expect(['Revoked', 'Inherited']).to.include(json.liensAccessStatus);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "If-Match", "value": "\"{{accessVersion}}\"" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"enabled\": false\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/users/{{userId}}/access",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "users", "{{userId}}", "access"]
            },
            "description": "Permission: `SYNQ_LIENS.user_access:manage`. Removes direct SynqLien roles but never deactivates the global user."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Grant Direct Product Access",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Direct access granted', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "const etag = pm.response.headers.get('ETag');",
                  "pm.environment.set('accessVersion', etag ? etag.replace(/W\\//i, '').replace(/\"/g, '') : json.accessVersion);",
                  "pm.expect(json.liensAccessStatus).to.eql('Granted');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "If-Match", "value": "\"{{accessVersion}}\"" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"enabled\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/users/{{userId}}/access",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "users", "{{userId}}", "access"]
            },
            "description": "Re-grants direct product access. Assign a role afterward if the user needs business capabilities."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "05 - Invitation Cancellation",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Invite Cancellation Target",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.environment.get('cancelTargetEmail')) {",
                  "  pm.environment.set('cancelTargetEmail', `postman.liens.cancel.${Date.now()}@example.test`);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Cancellation target invited', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.expect(json.invitationId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "pm.environment.set('cancelInvitationId', json.invitationId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{cancelTargetEmail}}\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Cancel\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Target\",\n  \"phone\": null,\n  \"roleCodes\": [\"SYNQLIEN_SELLER\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/invitations",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "invitations"]
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel Invitation",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Invitation cancelled', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{identityBaseUrl}}/api/v1/products/SYNQ_LIENS/user-management/invitations/{{cancelInvitationId}}",
              "host": ["{{identityBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "products", "SYNQ_LIENS", "user-management", "invitations", "{{cancelInvitationId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes a pending invitation; it is never physically deleted."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
